<WikiLayout title="WARDOGS Vehicle Compare" description="Compare WARDOGS vehicle battlefield roles and open connected entity references." canonicalPath="/tools/vehicle-compare/" pageType="WebApplication" showAd={true} adPlacement="tool">
  <p class="eyebrow">TOOL / VEHICLES</p><h1>Vehicle Compare</h1><p>Compare battlefield purpose before spending persistent cash. Transport, air mobility and heavy pressure require different crew plans and routes.</p><ToolShell tool="Vehicle comparison" description="Select two vehicles to compare their high-level battlefield roles and related guides." leftLabel="Vehicle A" rightLabel="Vehicle B" options={['URAL','URAL Defender','MH-6','UH-1Y','L2A6','SPH-2']}/><div class="inline-link-row"><a href="/database/vehicles/">Vehicles database</a><a href="/money/logistics/">Logistics guide</a></div>
  <section><h2>Compare the mission, not only the platform</h2><p>First decide whether the team needs transport, supply movement, air access or direct armored pressure. Then compare the crew burden and the guides connected to each vehicle. A powerful platform used without a route or crew plan can consume cash without improving the objective.</p><h2>Data limits</h2><p>Exact armor, speed, capacity or price values appear only when adequately supported. Otherwise they remain <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong>. Use the full entity page for current notes and patch history.</p></section>
  <section><h2>What to review after comparing</h2><p>Confirm that the selected platform can reach the intended route, that enough players are available to operate it, and that its role still matches the current objective. Consider how the vehicle will be recovered, resupplied or replaced if the plan fails. For transport-focused decisions, connect the comparison to the <a href="/money/logistics/">Logistics Guide</a> and current team movement.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is a heavier vehicle always better?</h3><p>No. Travel distance, crew availability, objective pressure and replacement risk all affect the choice.</p><h3>Where should new drivers begin?</h3><p>Review <a href="/vehicles/ground/">Ground Vehicles</a> and the <a href="/money/logistics/">Logistics Guide</a> before committing to a specialized platform.</p><p><a href="/compare/">Browse evidence-aware vehicle comparison pages →</a></p></section>
</WikiLayout>
